  "caveats": [
    "404 keyframes from 10 scenes is a very small corpus for a language model; the val numbers should be read as a sanity check that the data path is now correct, not as a competitive result.",
    "Trained from scratch rather than from pretrained GPT-2 weights: huggingface.co is blocked by egress policy in both available environments, and the repo's local GPT-2 is the degenerate checkpoint this replaces.",
    "Absolute waypoints, not residuals on a prior -- so it is compared against constant velocity, which is the prior it does not get."
  ],
  "val_examples_note": "Best, median and worst of the 58 held-out keyframes where the ego is actually moving (>2 m/s). Stationary samples are excluded because a parked car makes every predictor look perfect and shows nothing."
}